senses.gloss:
आ-√ रम् P. -रमति (Pāṇ. i, 3, 83), to pause, stop;
to leave off, AitBr.; ĀśvŚr.; Mn.; MBh.; Kathās. &c.;
to delight in;
to enjoy one's self, take pleasure, Mn.; Daś.; Kathās. &c.

अरं—√ कृ (Subj. -क॑रत् or -करत्, 1. pl. -कृष्णवाम; Imper. 1. sg. -करण् aor. 3. pl. -अ॑क्रन्)
to prepare, make ready, RV.;
to serve (with or without dat.), RV.

आ-√ रभ् P. (only pf. 1. pl. -ररभ्मा॑, RV. viii, 45, 20) Ā. -रभते (pf. -रेभे, &c.; Inf. -र॑भम् and -र॑भे, RV.)
to lay or take hold of, keep fast, cling to, RV.; AV.; ŚBr. &c.;
to gain a footing;
to enter, reach, attain, RV.;
to undertake, commence, begin, TBr.; ŚBr.; MBh.; Ragh.; Kathās. &c.;
to make, produce;
to form, compose, BhP. &c.:
Intens. (pf. आ॑-र॑रभे) to cling to, RV. i, 168, 3.

आरागय Nom. P. ˚यति, to gladden highly, Vajracch.;
to obtain, Lalit.;
to relish, Divyāv.

आ-√ राध् Caus. P. -राधयति, to conciliate, propitiate;
to strive to obtain the favour of or gain a boon from;
to solicit;
to honour, worship;
to deserve, merit, MBh.; R.; Megh.; Śak.; Kathās. &c.:
Pass. -राध्यते, to be effected or accomplished, Daś.
